@page "/docs/troubleshooting/form-name"
@attribute [FollowsModeSwitch]

@* A static post finds its form by FormName and its model by [SupplyParameterFromForm]'s FormName:
   no name is a 400, a different name binds nothing, a form that isn't rendered for the post is a
   400. Each checked against the site in Development; the fix in form-two-forms in all three modes. *@

<ArticlePage Section="troubleshooting" Slug="form-name">
    <Lead>
        Give each form a <Code>FormName</Code>, put the same name on its model's <Code>[SupplyParameterFromForm]</Code>,
        and render the form when the post comes in.
    </Lead>
    <ChildContent>
        <Heading Level="2">Problem</Heading>
        <TextBlock>A form works on interactive pages, but on <Anchor Href="docs/common/render-modes">static pages</Anchor> submitting it goes wrong in one of three ways:</TextBlock>
        <List Gap="2">
            <ListItem>
                The form post fails with 400 Bad Request: "The POST request does not specify which form is being submitted."
            </ListItem>
            <ListItem>
                The form post succeeds, but the fields come back empty and validation says required fields are missing, though
                they were filled in.
            </ListItem>
            <ListItem>
                The form post fails with 400 Bad Request: "Cannot submit the form 'profile' because no form on the page currently
                has that name."
            </ListItem>
        </List>
        <TextBlock>In production the 400 has no message; run in Development to see it.</TextBlock>

        <Heading Level="2">Cause</Heading>
        <TextBlock>
            On static pages, a form post is a new request. Blazor renders the page again, finds the form the post names,
            and fills the model from the posted fields. Each step goes by name:
        </TextBlock>
        <List Gap="2">
            <ListItem>
                <strong>No <Code>FormName</Code>.</strong> The form posts no name, so Blazor can't tell which form was
                submitted. Interactive pages don't post, so the form never needed one there.
            </ListItem>
            <ListItem>
                <strong>Different names.</strong> <Code>[SupplyParameterFromForm(FormName = "...")]</Code> fills the model
                only from the form with that name. With another name, the model isn't filled and the page creates an empty
                one.
            </ListItem>
            <ListItem>
                <strong>The form isn't there.</strong> The form is shown only after something the form post doesn't carry,
                such as a field set by an earlier post. The page Blazor renders for the form post has no form with that
                name.
            </ListItem>
        </List>

        <Heading Level="2">Fix</Heading>
        <TextBlock>
            Name the form, and give its model the same name:
        </TextBlock>
        <Code Block Language="razor" Title="Profile.razor" HighlightLines="1,7">@Fixed</Code>
        <TextBlock>
            On a page with two forms, give each form a name of its own, and its model the same name. Each form post then fills only its own
            model. This demo has a search form and a sign-up form on one page:
        </TextBlock>
        <ExampleViewer Example="form-two-forms" ModeSwitch />
        <TextBlock>
            Without <Code>FormName</Code>, <Code>[SupplyParameterFromForm]</Code> accepts a form post from any form on the
            page. Name it whenever the page has more than one form.
        </TextBlock>
        <TextBlock>
            When a form appears only in some states, keep that state where the form post can see it. Keep it in the URL,
            since the form posts back to the same URL, with its query. Or keep it in the posted fields.
        </TextBlock>

        <Heading Level="2">Related</Heading>
        <List Gap="2">
            <ListItem><Anchor Href="docs/components/form">Form</Anchor>: posting and submitting.</ListItem>
            <ListItem><Anchor Href="docs/common/forms">Forms and validation</Anchor>: a form that posts.</ListItem>
            <ListItem><Anchor Href="docs/troubleshooting/state-between-requests">A value resets on the next request</Anchor>: where a static page keeps its state.</ListItem>
        </List>
    </ChildContent>
</ArticlePage>

@code {
    private const string Fixed = """
        <Form Model="Model" FormName="profile" OnValidSubmit="SaveAsync">
            <TextField @bind-Value="Model!.Name" />
            <Button Submit>Save</Button>
        </Form>

        @code {
            [SupplyParameterFromForm(FormName = "profile")]
            private ProfileModel? Model { get; set; }

            protected override void OnInitialized() => Model ??= new();
        }
        """;
}
